\text{Time spent biking} = \frac{20}{2x+1} \text{ hours}
\]
\[
\text{Time spent running} = \frac{5}{x} \text{ hours}
\]
\[
\text{Total time} = \frac{20}{2x+1} + \frac{5}{x} + \frac{5}{60} = 110/60 \text{ hours}
\]
Simplifying the right-hand side, we get \[
\frac{20}{2x+1} + \frac{5}{x} + \frac{1}{12} = \frac{110}{60} = \frac{11}{6}
\]
We can now solve this equation for \(x\). We'll use Python to find the numerical solution. </think> <answer> 6.39 </answer>

